{"How are things with your new colleague?": "audio/clips/1ddccedf8eb3.mp3", "Pretty good. She's very reliable, and I find it easy to talk to her. We have quite a lot in common, so we get along surprisingly well.": "audio/clips/afef78f0919f.mp3", "That's nice. What do you have in common?": "audio/clips/b8eade0af2bf.mp3", "Is there anything you can't stand at work?": "audio/clips/380e8b3d5623.mp3", "Honestly, I can't stand people who constantly interrupt others. I can put up with it once or twice, but it becomes really frustrating when it happens in every meeting. However, I try to react calmly.": "audio/clips/4c0c0a359f83.mp3", "I know what you mean. How do you handle it?": "audio/clips/3bc32d10d184.mp3", "acquaintance": "audio/clips/5695170f672c.mp3", "reliable": "audio/clips/c5e8cfa79b53.mp3", "get along with": "audio/clips/094de84ee009.mp3", "in common": "audio/clips/b5a5dcbef532.mp3", "easy to talk to": "audio/clips/2d8fffd7dd87.mp3", "Mai always does what she promises. She's very ______.": "audio/clips/545b41c852fc.mp3", "considerate": "audio/clips/6271c4b65000.mp3", "easy-going": "audio/clips/b28d872db553.mp3", "Ben is relaxed and rarely gets upset. He's quite ______.": "audio/clips/d20a8810796a.mp3", "Linh notices when other people need help. She's very ______.": "audio/clips/ac8f99ec928d.mp3", "I know James from a course, but we aren't close friends. He's an ______.": "audio/clips/81aeefd8ce02.mp3", "I really like my new manager. We ______ each other very well.": "audio/clips/002c7b1a2d12.mp3", "can't stand": "audio/clips/5129f8b266a0.mp3", "put up with": "audio/clips/672335868491.mp3", "lose touch with": "audio/clips/ef18eca2b8e0.mp3", "I ______ people who interrupt all the time. It drives me crazy.": "audio/clips/75fb97c5e57d.mp3", "The noise is annoying, but I can ______ it for another hour.": "audio/clips/52d546825e1b.mp3", "We used to be close, but we gradually ______ each other after graduation.": "audio/clips/fb6c18a61eae.mp3", "got along with": "audio/clips/1003085b7978.mp3", "lost touch with": "audio/clips/78633f43a6ee.mp3", "I can't stand to wait in long lines.": "audio/clips/4c14e9bf3504.mp3", "I find easy to talk to her.": "audio/clips/c7b4475dff46.mp3", "I like people who listen carefully.": "audio/clips/19e3252bc2af.mp3", "We have a lot in common.": "audio/clips/9d0cda2eb1ce.mp3", "Talk about people in your work or daily life. Describe someone you get along with. Mention one behaviour you can't stand or have to put up with. Ask your partner at least two related questions.": "audio/clips/463ecfc21d4d.mp3", "Choose 6 target expressions. Write one true sentence with each.": "audio/clips/7b92a4e24f30.mp3", "What kind of people do you find easy or difficult to get along with? Include one reason, one example, and one sentence with who or that.": "audio/clips/3492a393d28c.mp3", "Honestly, I can't stand unnecessary meetings. They waste a lot of time mainly because nothing gets decided. For example, some meetings could be replaced with a short email. However, I don't mind meetings that have a clear purpose. In my experience, a short agenda makes a meeting worth the time.": "audio/clips/66d48c7f43ce.mp3", "Honestly": "audio/clips/e7d98cb22569.mp3", "However": "audio/clips/1c9d9af883f4.mp3", "For example": "audio/clips/dc3c09a115b4.mp3", "mainly": "audio/clips/6cac58e64448.mp3", "Is there anything you can't stand at work or in daily life?": "audio/clips/a3a5a4cd3400.mp3", "interrupt": "audio/clips/691911bb26d8.mp3", "complain": "audio/clips/6a91578231ef.mp3", "arrive late": "audio/clips/519df6ea4b8e.mp3", "speak rudely": "audio/clips/22f3f0d8b228.mp3", "make unnecessary noise": "audio/clips/efb0d9bdf6e1.mp3", "What kind of person do you find easy to get along with?": "audio/clips/a247e15aba4e.mp3", "open-minded": "audio/clips/90748e6189af.mp3", "listen carefully": "audio/clips/73aa8453de45.mp3", "communicate clearly": "audio/clips/850c8cf6eb18.mp3", "a close friend": "audio/clips/ef9662251efa.mp3", "an acquaintance": "audio/clips/565954eae4c3.mp3", "an easy-going colleague": "audio/clips/b9caa6c05d3e.mp3", "a reliable person": "audio/clips/677af097288e.mp3", "a difficult person": "audio/clips/86a6b148c884.mp3", "someone you lost touch with": "audio/clips/38abe46867f2.mp3", "You look surprised. Is everything okay?": "audio/clips/aa7ee430361d.mp3", "Yes. I just got a message from Sophie, an old university friend.": "audio/clips/d4dd4abe686a.mp3", "I don't think you've mentioned her before. Were you close?": "audio/clips/ed5fbc01c752.mp3", "Very close. We used to spend nearly every weekend together.": "audio/clips/b691985b29e0.mp3", "What happened? Did you have an argument?": "audio/clips/93c139af4efa.mp3", "No. We moved to different cities and gradually drifted apart.": "audio/clips/edb7f7680ead.mp3", "So why did she message you now?": "audio/clips/efcc8029feb2.mp3", "She found an old photo of us and decided to reach out.": "audio/clips/028436166a76.mp3", "That's nice. Are you going to get back in touch properly?": "audio/clips/1708d95f1322.mp3", "Definitely. We're planning a video call this weekend so we can catch up.": "audio/clips/2d6b416e26f3.mp3", "Do you think it'll feel awkward after so long?": "audio/clips/59352072d494.mp3", "Maybe at first, but I think we'll quickly pick up where we left off.": "audio/clips/a34c8847e360.mp3", "You and Carla used to be really close. Do you still talk?": "audio/clips/27e1c0c255a0.mp3", "We do, but not as often as before. We both have a lot going on.": "audio/clips/ce00329e8119.mp3", "Is it mainly work, or have your lives just changed?": "audio/clips/031caccbd210.mp3", "A bit of both. She has two young children, and my job has become busier.": "audio/clips/6b7f3731c445.mp3", "Does it bother you that you don't speak regularly?": "audio/clips/afda5fa87953.mp3", "Sometimes. I miss our long conversations, especially when I need advice.": "audio/clips/c52f1c2daca9.mp3", "Have you told her that?": "audio/clips/48b3756efec9.mp3", "Not directly. I know she's busy, so I don't want to make her feel guilty.": "audio/clips/86f751320bb2.mp3", "Maybe you could suggest something simple, like a monthly call.": "audio/clips/96a79cec84a8.mp3", "That might work. It would help us stay connected without adding pressure.": "audio/clips/42e47b84726e.mp3", "Exactly. Good friendships still need time, even when life gets busy.": "audio/clips/1ca7b1e3f83c.mp3", "You're right. I'll reach out tonight and see when she's free.": "audio/clips/d4b0282fc546.mp3", "We don't meet often, but we ______ by texting every few weeks.": "audio/clips/02b4f364b513.mp3", "keep in touch": "audio/clips/f78d453b821a.mp3", "reach out": "audio/clips/f8277f02f0f6.mp3", "catch up": "audio/clips/c270cbef8991.mp3", "make time for": "audio/clips/bc33b846358f.mp3", "I haven't spoken to Lan in months. I should ______ to her.": "audio/clips/79528a26e378.mp3", "We had coffee yesterday and ______ on everything that had happened.": "audio/clips/7a1b08411f56.mp3", "kept in touch": "audio/clips/497e4ff96113.mp3", "reached out": "audio/clips/0e6b8d3fe74f.mp3", "caught up": "audio/clips/9377e59717c7.mp3", "made time for": "audio/clips/4a9195c09483.mp3", "Even when I'm busy, I try to ______ the people I care about.": "audio/clips/1ba498b157f0.mp3", "We were once close, but we slowly ______ after university.": "audio/clips/316a89b7cfd9.mp3", "drifted apart": "audio/clips/293155d0c35d.mp3", "got back in touch": "audio/clips/26a8e99f52ec.mp3", "stayed connected": "audio/clips/bcf5f5083128.mp3", "I'd love to ______ with my old roommate.": "audio/clips/d3e269e3f7cc.mp3", "drift apart": "audio/clips/9bb55ee33573.mp3", "get back in touch": "audio/clips/03c8430b7624.mp3", "stay connected": "audio/clips/b7652f2098aa.mp3", "have a lot going on": "audio/clips/d55146174c1a.mp3", "She hasn't replied because she ______ at the moment.": "audio/clips/992bd05391a8.mp3", "has a lot going on": "audio/clips/f023144506ce.mp3", "Even though we live far apart, we still ______ online.": "audio/clips/57dd292dcbe0.mp3", "a lot going on": "audio/clips/e432dbcf026e.mp3", "We've stayed ______ for years.": "audio/clips/4188ed8a64d5.mp3", "in touch": "audio/clips/831601a21392.mp3", "on touch": "audio/clips/32148d4d8620.mp3", "with touch": "audio/clips/e531d6d7b91d.mp3", "touch": "audio/clips/f4d1f0193879.mp3", "I finally reached out ______ her.": "audio/clips/75f59163f8fa.mp3", "for": "audio/clips/43eef9a62abb.mp3", "to": "audio/clips/4374aaee247f.mp3", "with": "audio/clips/8fcd25a39d20.mp3", "on": "audio/clips/db3d405b1067.mp3", "I caught up ______ Minh yesterday.": "audio/clips/dd2655736eff.mp3", "We gradually drifted apart ______ each other.": "audio/clips/d3f828c729ad.mp3", "from": "audio/clips/0b1e95cfd977.mp3", "I make time ______ close friends.": "audio/clips/0c1656397b30.mp3", "Talk about how your relationships have changed over time. Share one person you have stayed in touch with. Talk about someone you drifted apart from or reconnected with. Respond to your partner and ask at least three follow-up questions.": "audio/clips/aebc04686f7a.mp3", "How have one of your friendships changed over time? Include: how you met · what you used to do · how you stay connected now · one future plan.": "audio/clips/2a10326cb9de.mp3", "Choose 8 expressions from L01–L02. Make one true sentence with each.": "audio/clips/dd7a60a8b11e.mp3", "What is a realistic way for busy friends to stay connected?": "audio/clips/504174e0edba.mp3", "pick up where we left off": "audio/clips/b9532dc01740.mp3", "When we finally meet, we usually ______, as if no time has passed.": "audio/clips/ef15c38392a7.mp3", "make someone feel guilty": "audio/clips/8d7470ea9b48.mp3", "without adding pressure": "audio/clips/e084dabbafa3.mp3", "reach out tonight": "audio/clips/c27f9fd7d53b.mp3", "I found a great hotel for our weekend trip. It's right in the city centre.": "audio/clips/830e32bf3a06.mp3", "It looks nice, but I don't think we should spend that much.": "audio/clips/fa72d7b040e3.mp3", "Really? I think the location will save us a lot of time.": "audio/clips/cc004f34f087.mp3", "I see your point, but we'll only be there for two nights.": "audio/clips/6a0aa0da3298.mp3", "True, although I don't want to stay somewhere uncomfortable.": "audio/clips/b49fa74ad539.mp3", "Neither do I. We could find a cheaper place nearby.": "audio/clips/dde040547cd2.mp3", "You have a point. What price range do you have in mind?": "audio/clips/3d26b9da0f94.mp3", "Maybe something under two million a night. Would that work?": "audio/clips/e1e62d042cfd.mp3", "Possibly. I'm open to staying outside the centre if the transport is good.": "audio/clips/a671e54c38e4.mp3", "Fair enough. We can compare travel time as well as price.": "audio/clips/13b82a83dff9.mp3", "Okay. Let's each choose two places and look at them tonight.": "audio/clips/605d005c4548.mp3", "Perfect. I'm sure we can work it out.": "audio/clips/8327603b651e.mp3", "Ben, can I bring something up? The kitchen has been quite messy lately.": "audio/clips/98198263529c.mp3", "I know. Work has been exhausting, so I haven't cleaned much this week.": "audio/clips/4f252ddf6d94.mp3", "I understand, but I can't keep doing all of it by myself.": "audio/clips/2bbb47661859.mp3", "That's fair. I didn't realise you were doing most of the cleaning.": "audio/clips/e354b0c10af0.mp3", "I didn't say anything because I wanted to avoid an argument.": "audio/clips/34655cc9e914.mp3", "I wish you had told me earlier. We could have worked it out.": "audio/clips/788ed29a7f48.mp3", "You're right. Could we make a simple cleaning schedule?": "audio/clips/2fa1b934a749.mp3", "I'm open to that, although I don't want it to be too strict.": "audio/clips/7f6ee8079aa8.mp3", "Fair enough. How about we each choose the jobs we don't mind doing?": "audio/clips/fbb0d38a8324.mp3", "That sounds reasonable. I can cook and take out the rubbish.": "audio/clips/3d2b6eef7d38.mp3", "Great. I'll do the shopping, and we can share the rest.": "audio/clips/83dfd6526e8f.mp3", "Deal. If something bothers us, let's bring it up sooner.": "audio/clips/eaff5543fd6c.mp3", "Personal response: Is it better to bring up a small problem immediately?": "audio/clips/bab1ebc641c9.mp3", "I ______ you about the price. It is too expensive.": "audio/clips/bd5975beb589.mp3", "agree with": "audio/clips/b0fcb2189e0e.mp3", "disagree with": "audio/clips/35019184f6ab.mp3", "have a point": "audio/clips/4b0e2c11dc05.mp3", "not necessarily": "audio/clips/d2aa54e3ffdc.mp3", "I ______ that idea because it would create more work.": "audio/clips/ead940202f2c.mp3", "see your point": "audio/clips/97605578dfa1.mp3", "You ______. We should check the details before deciding.": "audio/clips/f6c6d53ce1e0.mp3", "I can ______, but I still feel differently.": "audio/clips/26c84692bf31.mp3", "Something has been bothering me, so I need to ______ calmly.": "audio/clips/47515fd60950.mp3", "bring it up": "audio/clips/a847c4acf43f.mp3", "work it out": "audio/clips/7d740e981e53.mp3", "compromise": "audio/clips/faaabf119c69.mp3", "be open to": "audio/clips/d5d4746cac8c.mp3", "We disagree, but I'm sure we can ______ together.": "audio/clips/66167a6c64df.mp3", "change my mind": "audio/clips/b0a23b3fc41d.mp3", "Neither option is perfect. We may need to ______.": "audio/clips/c600c067dea6.mp3", "Your example is convincing. It might ______.": "audio/clips/fa20ec5fcb1f.mp3", "I'm not sure I agree.": "audio/clips/a8b780fcd617.mp3", "You don't understand.": "audio/clips/9d94b2a0e093.mp3", "No.": "audio/clips/b8b9f1367ad6.mp3", "That won't work.": "audio/clips/356fb23c5083.mp3", "I'm not sure that would work.": "audio/clips/dfb718ecdf1f.mp3", "Do this instead.": "audio/clips/6730304cc2e6.mp3", "That's wrong.": "audio/clips/042c168abc0b.mp3", "I may not have explained my point clearly.": "audio/clips/1c0080fa2cec.mp3", "Could we try another option?": "audio/clips/f0c5a14e8d02.mp3", "I'm open to ______ it once.": "audio/clips/e121a183aeeb.mp3", "try": "audio/clips/3240aa0fe3ca.mp3", "trying": "audio/clips/d33f85fc81c5.mp3", "tried": "audio/clips/c4832b3644bb.mp3", "tries": "audio/clips/77fbc933f6d3.mp3", "We could compromise ______ the price.": "audio/clips/9823da60becf.mp3", "I need to bring ______ up calmly.": "audio/clips/66958fd85f91.mp3", "that": "audio/clips/33b82201081e.mp3", "it": "audio/clips/6c5522ca8af8.mp3", "this one": "audio/clips/ac1ebf971f8c.mp3", "them": "audio/clips/98910a6e9ae7.mp3", "Choose one real-life decision on which you may disagree. State your view and explain why. Acknowledge one point from your partner. Ask at least two follow-up questions. Agree on a compromise or explain why you cannot agree yet.": "audio/clips/8ff8846dfa36.mp3", "Describe a disagreement that ended well. What helped? Include: the issue · both views · one useful response · the final solution.": "audio/clips/8fcd77be22cb.mp3", "Choose 8 items from L03. Make one true or realistic sentence with each.": "audio/clips/041aca093cfb.mp3", "People should never discuss serious issues by text.": "audio/clips/ba18e724373c.mp3", "'Is working from home always easier?' '______. It depends on your home.'": "audio/clips/79cf92c8945d.mp3", "You have a point": "audio/clips/6713b3d2b3e7.mp3", "I agree with": "audio/clips/e79cea606c7e.mp3", "I don't love the idea, but I'm ______ trying it once.": "audio/clips/40c0000aa87b.mp3", "open to": "audio/clips/49b06c25a596.mp3", "bring something up": "audio/clips/bb7e79ce9c1b.mp3", "by myself": "audio/clips/bc3bff740049.mp3", "avoid an argument": "audio/clips/7f1962cb2aca.mp3", "too strict": "audio/clips/9c381cfeb388.mp3", "sound reasonable": "audio/clips/64a59a844926.mp3", "colleague": "audio/clips/ace6752be4cc.mp3", "I have a meeting with my colleague.": "audio/clips/8f19fd68a5e8.mp3", "My colleague is very helpful.": "audio/clips/b551963e17e5.mp3", "He's just an acquaintance, not a close friend.": "audio/clips/2ddbb465b76c.mp3", "I met an acquaintance at the conference.": "audio/clips/5bb481fa379e.mp3", "She's very reliable — always on time.